   "evidence": "Line 332: `W.pathLink (staplePath (x + v + w - y) (-w) y x) = (W.pathLink (staplePath v w x y))\u207b\u00b9`; proof is `rw [\u2190 reverse_staplePath, pathLink_reverse]` (line 333), i.e. it is exactly the reverse-path statement. In Mathlib `_swap` denotes literal argument exchange (`Prod.swap`, `Equiv.swap`, `Function.swap`), which is not what happens here.",
